Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:16:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7325-nothing-spacewar: map the WCD9385
 DMIC port to its own SoundWire port

tx-port-mapping <1 2 2 4> put the codec DMIC0-3/MBHC port on master port 2, together with ADC3/ADC4,
so the two collided (the SWR_MIC inputs of port 2 carried garbage). The phone microphones are digital:
stock Android maps DMIC0 (handset) to SWRM_TX3_CH1 and DMIC3 (speakerphone) to SWRM_TX3_CH4, i.e.
master port 3. Use <1 2 3 4>, as Fairphone 5 does with the same codec on the same SoC.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
index 5f148d3ec..85e25ad1d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
@@ -1725,7 +1725,7 @@ wcd_tx: codec@0,3 {
 		compatible = "sdw20217010d00";
 		reg = <0 3>;
 
-		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <1 2 2 4>;
+		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <1 2 3 4>;
 	};
 };
 
